Political Spending
Scope & Core Inquiries: How transparent and ethical is this company's political spending, lobbying, and government relations strategy? What scale of financial contributions does it direct toward politicians, political action committees (PACs, Super PACs), party committees, and ballot initiatives? Does it channel "dark money" through 501(c)(4) non-profits, right-wing think tanks, or industry trade associations to covertly shape legislation and regulatory policy? Is there a severe disconnect between the company’s public marketing/ESG commitments and the actual records of lawmakers or ballot initiatives it finances (e.g., championing sustainability publicly while financing politicians who block climate legislation)? Does it exploit the "revolving door" by hiring former lawmakers or agency regulators to lobby on its behalf? Make sure to include the specific causes that are supported and opposed.